    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but isn't it basically impossible to enforce those things? like, if a country says they are being \"transparent\" but they are the only ones who decide what a \"threat\" is, there's no real accountability. most of the time, \"proportionality\" is just whatever the government says it is. isn't it more realistic to say that once you give a state the power to gatekeep the internet for \"security,\" you've basically guaranteed they'll eventually use it to control the narrative?",
